            </button>
            <button class="ch-toolbar-button" title="Modified" onclick="modifyAction()">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path d="M3 17.25V21h3.75L17.81 9.94l-3.75-3.75L3 17.25zM20.71 7.04c.39-.39.39-1.02 0-1.41l-2.34-2.34c-.39-.39-1.02-.39-1.41 0l-1.83 1.83 3.75 3.75 1.83-1.83z"></path>
                </svg>
            </button>
        </div>

       <div class="ch">

    <h1>Schmitt Trigger with BJTs (Emitter-Coupled)</h1>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">This is the classic <strong>two-transistor Schmitt trigger</strong>. Q1 and Q2 share one emitter resistor <strong>Re</strong>, and the collector of Q1 drives the base of Q2 through the divider R1/R2. This coupling is a <strong>positive feedback</strong> loop, so the circuit has <strong>two different switching thresholds</strong>: the input must rise above an upper threshold to switch the output up, and fall below a lower threshold to switch it back. The gap between them is the <strong>hysteresis</strong>. It turns a slow sine wave into a clean, fast-edged square wave and ignores noise smaller than the gap.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Circuit Components</h2>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>Vcc = 12 V:</strong> DC supply.</li>
            <li><strong>Vin:</strong> sine source, 3.5 V amplitude with a 4.4 V offset at 1 kHz, so it swings from 0.9 V to 7.9 V and crosses both thresholds. It starts at its minimum (phase −90°) so the initial state is clear.</li>
            <li><strong>Q1:</strong> input transistor (NPN). Its base receives Vin.</li>
            <li><strong>Q2:</strong> output transistor (NPN). Its base is the node <em>b2</em>, taken from the divider R1/R2.</li>
            <li><strong>Rc1 = 2.2 KΩ, Rc2 = 1 KΩ:</strong> collector resistors. The output is taken at the collector of Q2 (node <em>out</em>).</li>
            <li><strong>R1 = 1.5 KΩ, R2 = 3.3 KΩ:</strong> coupling divider from the collector of Q1 (node <em>c1</em>) to the base of Q2.</li>
            <li><strong>Re = 1 KΩ:</strong> common emitter resistor (node <em>e</em>). It creates the feedback that produces the hysteresis.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>How the Circuit Works</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">
        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>State A: Q1 off, Q2 on (output low)</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Vin is low, so Q1 is off and its collector is pulled up through Rc1.</li>
                <li>The divider gives Q2 a base voltage of about <span><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;">V</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.2222em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">b</span><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.1963em; vertical-align: -0.836em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;">V</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.2222em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">cc</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3603em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0077em;">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0077em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">c</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0077em;">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0077em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0077em;">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0077em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="" style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span class="" style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0077em;">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0077em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.836em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">5.5</span><span class="mspace">&nbsp;</span><span class="mord mathrm" style="margin-right: 0.0139em;">V</span></span></span></span></span>, so Q2 conducts.</li>
                <li>Q2 current flows through Re and lifts the emitter to about <strong>4.9 V</strong>.</li>
                <li>The output is low, about <strong>7.15 V</strong>.</li>
                <li>Q1 only turns on when Vin reaches the emitter voltage plus about 0.6 V, i.e. the <strong>upper threshold</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>State B: Q1 on, Q2 off (output high)</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>When Q1 turns on, its collector falls, which lowers the base of Q2 and turns Q2 off.</li>
                <li>With Q2 off, no current flows in Rc2, so the output rises to <strong>12 V</strong>.</li>
                <li>Now only Q1 current flows through Re, and the emitter drops to about <strong>2.7 V</strong>, below its value in State A.</li>
                <li>So Vin must fall much lower than before to switch back: this is the <strong>lower threshold</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p style="line-height: 1.6;">The change of the emitter voltage between the two states is what separates the thresholds. The output is <strong>non-inverting</strong>: when Vin goes high the output goes high.</p>

    <h2>Simulation Results (Transient, 0 - 3 ms)</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">
        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>Thresholds</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Upper threshold (output switches up): <strong>Vin ≈ 5.43 V</strong>.</li>
                <li>Lower threshold (output switches down): <strong>Vin ≈ 3.18 V</strong>.</li>
                <li>Hysteresis: <span><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;">V</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.2222em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0813em;">H</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7278em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">5.43</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">3.18</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord">2.25</span><span class="mspace">&nbsp;</span><span class="mord mathrm" style="margin-right: 0.0139em;">V</span></span></span></span></span>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>Output</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Square wave between about <strong>7.15 V</strong> (Q2 on) and <strong>12 V</strong> (Q2 off).</li>
                <li>Period 1 ms, the same frequency as the input.</li>
                <li>Switching happens at about 0.30 ms and 0.81 ms in each cycle.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card green-border">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">The two coupled BJTs act as a comparator with built-in hysteresis of about 2.25 V. Unlike the op-amp version, the output does not swing symmetrically around zero: its low level is set by the Q2 current through Rc2 and Re (about 7.15 V) and its high level is the supply (12 V). The thresholds depend on Re, Rc1, R1, R2 and Vcc, so they can be tuned by changing these resistors (the values quoted here are read from the simulation and vary by about 0.05 V with the time step). Typical uses are noise-free level detection, waveform shaping and switch debouncing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Try It Yourself</h2>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            <li>Run the <strong>transient analysis</strong> and compare the <strong>in</strong> and <strong>out</strong> curves.</li>
            <li>Increase Re to 1.5 KΩ: the lower threshold rises to about 3.7 V, so the hysteresis shrinks to about 1.8 V, and the low output level rises to about 8.7 V.</li>
            <li>Increase Rc1 to 3.3 KΩ: both thresholds move down (to about 4.7 V and 2.5 V) while the hysteresis stays almost the same (about 2.2 V).</li>
            <li>Reduce the amplitude of Vin so it stays between the two thresholds: the output stops switching.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div>

    </div>
    </div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(381,40)" x="381" y="40" width="345" height="229" class="analysis" name="analysis" description="{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Time Domain&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;dcsweep&quot;:{&quot;param&quot;:&quot;Non&quot;,&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;stop&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;step&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:false},&quot;time&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;0s&quot;,&quot;stop&quot;:&quot;3ms&quot;,&quot;step&quot;:&quot;0.005ms&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:false},&quot;ac&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;stop&quot;:&quot;1000&quot;,&quot;step&quot;:&quot;100&quot;,&quot;scale&quot;:&quot;dec&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;de&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:false},&quot;yAxe&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;out&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#ea2e2e&quot;}],&quot;xAxe&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;in&quot;,&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#000000&quot;,&quot;used&quot;:true},&quot;layout&quot;:{&quot;margin&quot;:{&quot;l&quot;:35,&quot;r&quot;:25,&quot;b&quot;:80,&quot;t&quot;:35},&quot;font&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#333333&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:11,&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;},&quot;paper_bgcolor&quot;:&quot;#ffffff&quot;,&quot;plot_bgcolor&quot;:&quot;#f8f8f8&quot;,&quot;bordercolor&quot;:&quot;#cccccc&quot;,&quot;yaxis&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;linear&quot;,&quot;gridcolor&quot;:&quot;#e0e0e0&quot;,&quot;showgrid&quot;:true},&quot;xaxis&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;linear&quot;,&quot;gridcolor&quot;:&quot;#e0e0e0&quot;,&quot;showgrid&quot;:true},&quot;showlegend&quot;:true,&quot;grid&quot;:{&quot;rows&quot;:1,&quot;columns&quot;:1,&quot;pattern&quot;:&quot;independent&quot;,&quot;roworder&quot;:&quot;bottom to top&quot;}},&quot;options&quot;:{},&quot;sweep&quot;:{&quot;param&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;values&quot;:&quot;[]&quot;}}"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="345" height="229"><d